# Saves

Persist **only the versioned envelope**. There is one writer and one reader of
that format, and no second serialisation anywhere in the project.

**An unknown version parses to `null`. It never throws.** Malformed JSON, a
version from the future, a missing or mistyped field — all `null`.

A `null` is not an error the player is shown. It is a new run, quietly. A
corrupt save opens the Crossing, not a broken screen.

The envelope carries what a run is determined by — the seed and the death count
— because those are what make a maze layout reproducible (GENERATOR.md). It
also carries the **campaign ledger**, which is the whole point of there being
two (`.llm/rules/ledgers.mdc`): a save that loses the dice you collected has
lost the game, even if it loads.
